      "writtenOn": "2024-04-29T17:02:03Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "For example:\n```\nif (foo)\n  ATRACE_ANDROID_FRAMEWORK_ALWAYS(\"My format with a number: %d\", myNum);\n```\n\nExpands to:\n```\nif (foo)\n  char skTraceStrBuf123[256];\n  snprintf(skTraceStrBuf123, 256,      \n           \"My format with a number: %d\", myNum);\n  TRACE_EVENT0_ALWAYS(\"skia.android\", TRACE_STR_COPY(skTraceStrBuf123));\n```\n\nWith only the first line being in scope of the `if`. That said, I\u0027m realizing that would cause a compilation error, but I\u0027d like to document it all the same.\n\nThe scariness factor hasn\u0027t changed, I just noticed it was undocumented. I\u0027ll mention it in the commit message.",
